# Siamese BERT – Requirement Pair Classification

A **Siamese MPNet-based model** for identifying semantic relationships between requirement pairs — classifying them as **Duplicate**, **Conflict**, or **Neutral**.

---

## Overview

This project fine-tunes a **Siamese BERT architecture (mpnet-base-v2)** for **requirement analysis**.
It helps detect overlapping, contradictory, or unrelated requirements in complex system specifications.

---

## Model Architecture

| Component               | Description                                    |             |                 |
| ----------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ----------- | --------------- |
| **Backbone**            | `mpnet-base-v2`                                |             |                 |
| **Pooling**             | Mean pooling                                   |             |                 |
| **Feature Combination** | `[emb1, emb2,                                  | emb1 - emb2 | , emb1 * emb2]` |
| **Classifier**          | 3 Fully Connected layers + BatchNorm + Dropout |             |                 |
| **Output Classes**      | `Duplicate`, `Conflict`, `Neutral`             |             |                 |

---

## Training Configuration

| Parameter     | Value                              |
| ------------- | ---------------------------------- |
| Dataset       | 29,999 requirement pairs           |
| Split         | 80% train / 20% validation         |
| Batch Size    | 16                                 |
| Learning Rate | 2e-5                               |
| Epochs        | 11                                 |
| Optimizer     | AdamW                              |
| Scheduler     | Linear Warmup & Decay              |
| Loss          | CrossEntropy (weighted)            |
| Framework     | PyTorch + HuggingFace Transformers |

---

## Results

| Metric                  | Score      |
| ----------------------- | ---------- |
| **Validation Accuracy** | **88.41%** |
| **Weighted F1 Score**   | **0.8808** |
| **Best Validation F1**  | **0.8842** |

**Per-class performance:**

| Label     | Precision | Recall | F1   | Support |
| --------- | --------- | ------ | ---- | ------- |
| Duplicate | 0.98      | 0.66   | 0.79 | 1823    |
| Conflict  | 0.76      | 0.99   | 0.86 | 2117    |
| Neutral   | 0.99      | 0.98   | 0.98 | 2059    |

